scSénatd2011e91-CourtaboeufgImpr. Seven  a1 vol. (33, 61 p.)cgraph.d24 cm19a[Impressions]h2011-2012fSénatvn° 48| aLes rapports du Sénatx1249-4356  aEnregistré à la présidence du Sénat le 19 octobre 2011  aEn appendice, rapport d\'enquête de la Cour des comptes sur "L\'agence de l\'outre-mer pour la mobilité" 0034283059tRapports du Sénat (Paris)x1249-4356d2011 0042581265tImpressions. 2011-2012 / Sénatv481 aL\'agence de l\'outre-mer pour la mobilitéeun pilotage à l\'aveugle ?||316576227aAgence de l\'outre-mer pour la mobilitécFrance2rameau  a354.091 71244v23  a3502Cadre de classement de la Bibliographie nationale française |312285287oISNI0000000081249748aPatientbGeorgesf1949-....4710 |312806529oISNI0000000121312044aDoligébÉricf1943-....4710||311864141oISNI0000000121513460aFrancebSénatc1958-....bCommission des finances4070 0aFRbFR-751131015c20111219gAFNORhFRBNF42568907000000X2intermrc  5FR-751131008:42568907001001a2011-323592b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Droit, économie, politique - MagasindO  5FR-751131008:42568907002001a064.351 SENA 11/48b759999999cTolbiac - Haut de Jardin - Droit, économie, politique - Salle D - Libre accèsdN04795cam  22003733  450 FRBNF427309240000009http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb427309242  a9781588394675  a1588394670bThe Metropolitan Museum of Art  a9780300184976  a0300184972bYale University Press  a9780300188578  a0300188579bYale UK  aOCoLC785864600  a20130131d20122012m  y0engy50      ba0 aeng  aUS  aa   z   00|y|  az1 aMatissebTexte impriméein search of true paintinge[exhibition, Centre Pompidou, Musee National d\'Art Moderne, Paris, Mar. 7-June 18, 2012, Statens Museum for Kunst, Copenhagen, July 14-Oct. 28, 2012, Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York, Dec. 4, 2012-Mar. 17, 2013]fedited by Dorthe Aagesen and Rebecca Rabinow  aNew YorkcMetropolitan Museum of Artd©2012  a1 vol. (XII-260 p.)cill. (some color), portraitsd28 cm  aBibliogr. p. 224-238. Index1 aDirector\'s Foreword ; Acknowledgments ;  Lenders to the Exhibition ;  Introduction / Dorthe Aagesen and Rebecca Rabinow ;  "A picture is like a game of cards" / Claudine Grammont ;  Impressionism in Question / Claudine Grammont ;  Blinded by the Sun / Alastair Wright ;  Cézanne versus Signac / Claudine Grammont ;  An Experiment in Deformation / Rebecca Rabinow and Isabelle Duvernois ;  The Academic Tradion Revised / Dorth Aagesen and Kathrine Segel ;  Model ; Bather ; Odalisque / Kasper Monrad ;  Inventing a Decorative Space / Cécile Debray ;  A Slight Shift in Perspective / Rebecca Rabinow and Isabelle Duvernois ;  A Garden "Redone Three Times" / Cécile Debray ;  Notre Dame between Heaven and Earth / Rémi Labrusse ;  Time Embodied / Jack Flam ;  Black Ribbon and Blue Stripes / Isabelle Monod-Fontaine ;  Supernatural Interiors / Cécile Debray ;  Surface and Depth / Stephanie D\'Alessandro ;  Laurette: Line and Color / Hilary Spurling ;  Painting the Light / Dorthe Aagesen ;  The Beach at Étretat / Rebecca Rabinow ;  Anemonism: "A Dreamy Treatment of Color" / Cécile Debray ;  Variations on the Odalisque / Isabelle Monod-Fontaine ;  The Eternal Feminine / Jack Flam ;  The Woman in Blue / Rebecca Rabinow ;  The Metaphysics of Decoration / Doïna Lemny ;  Toward a State of Pure Essence / Dorthe Aagesen ;  Painting as Film / Dorthe Aagesen ;  Themes and Variations / Samantha Rippner ;  Front Views / Cécile Debray ;  Radiant Color / Rebecca Rabinow ;  Notes ;  Works in the Exhibition / Compiled by Christel Hollevoet-Force and Mary Chan ;  Bibliography ;  Index ;  Photograph Credits ;  Contributions to the Catalogue.  a"Throughout his long career, Henri Matisse (1869-1954) continually expanded the boundaries of his art. By repeating images in pairs, trios, and series, he conducted an ongoing dialogue with his earlier works in order to, as he put it, "push further and deeper into true painting." In this fresh approach to a much-studied artist, prominent scholars from the United States and Europe examine more than sixty works in concise chapters that focus on this aspect of Matisse\'s working process. From early pairs such as Young Sailor I and II (1906) and Le Lexe I and II (1907-8) through a series of late studio scenes from Vence (1946-48). Matisse is shown revisiting a given theme with the aim of devising innovative, often radical, solutions to such problems as how to portray light, handle paint, select colors, and manipulate perspective. New technical studies of the early paired works and photographs documenting the evolution of his later paintings help to elucidate Matisse\'s complex evolution. In numerous excerpts from letter sand interviews, he is revealed as an artist who regularly questioned himself and his methods, a man of powerful intellect who regarded each new painting as an adventure. A significant addition to art historical literature, Matisse: In Search of True Painting is a revelatory study of a seminal figure in 20th-century modernism."--P. [4] of cover1 aExpositionmParisnCentre national d\'art et de culture Georges Pompidouj20121 aExpositionmCopenhaguenStatens museum for kunstj20121 aExpositionmNew YorknMetropolitan Museum of Artj2012 |311915136aMatissebHenrif1869-1954311938837xCatalogues d\'exposition2rameau |314565564oISNI0000000052121577aRabinowbRebecca A.4340 |313561384oISNI000000006653396XaAagesenbDorthef1966-....4340 3aUSbOCoLCc20130131h7858646002marc21 0bDLCgrda  5FR-751131010:42730924001001a2012-275819b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Littérature et art - MagasindO02186cam  2200337   450 FRBNF422584090000005http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb422584098  bBr.  aFRb01047095  a20100818d2010    m  h0frey50      ba0 afre  aFR  a||||z   00|y|  ar1 a2Hors-2DansbTexte impriméeproduction à 4 mains et parcours initiatique de Sergio Stern et Anne Bouyerecatalogue raisonnée[e