ce prud\'homale plus efficientebTexte impriméecomment développer conciliation et médiation en matière sociale ?erapport présenté au nom de la Commission de l\'emploi et des affaires sociales [de la Chambre de commerce et d\'industrie de Paris] et adopté par l\'Assemblée générale du 25 octobre 2012fpar monsieur Michel Laurentgavec le concours du Centre de médiation et d\'arbitrage de Parisgavec la collaboration de monsieur Renan Friederich,...  aPariscChambre de commerce et d\'industriedDL 2012  a1 vol. (27 p.)d26 cme1 synthèse| aRapports et prises de position de la CCIPx0995-4457 0034254804tRapport - Chambre de commerce et d\'industrie de Parisx0995-4457d2012  a3402Cadre de classement de la Bibliographie nationale française |316648459aLaurentbMichelf19..-....cmembre de la CCIP4710||311863084oISNI0000000122939359aChambre de commerce et d\'industrie de région Paris Île-de-France4070 0aFRbFR-751131015c20121130gAFNORhFRBNF42801202000000X2intermrc  5FR-751131008:42801202001001a2012-345009b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Droit, économie, politique - MagasindO04427cam  22004213  450 FRBNF427164200000002http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb42716420b  a978-0-300-17636-0  a0-300-17636-8brel.  aOCoLC711045490  a20140108d2011    m  y0engy50      ba0 aeng  aUS  aa   z   00|y|  az1 aArt of armorbTexte impriméesamurai armor from the Ann and Gabriel Barbier-Mueller museume[exhibition, Musée du quai Branly, Paris, November 8, 2011 - January 29, 2012, Musée de la civilisation, Québec, April 4, 2012 - January 27, 2013]fessays by Morihiro Ogawa ... [et al.]gcatalog text by Bernard Fournier-Bourdiergedited by J. Gabriel Barbier-Mueller  aDallas (Tex.)cthe Ann and Gabriel Barbier-Mueller museumaNew Haven (Conn.)cYale university pressdcop. 2011  a1 vol. (359 p.)cill. en coul., cartesd32 cm  aNotes bibliogr.  aAutre forme de titre : Samurai armor from the Ann and Gabriel Barbier-Mueller Museum1 aCollector\'s story / Gabriel Barbier-MuelleraInterview with Ann and Gabriel Barbier-MuelleraIntroduction : Japanese armor deconstructed / Morihiro OgawaaThe warrior in Japanese history /John StevensonaThe roles of women of the Samurai class / Sachiko HoriaArmor of wood and stone : castles of the Samurai /Stephen TurnbullaKawai Kabuto : helmets "transformed" / John AndersonaHorse accoutrements and mounted warfare / Ian BottomleyaArms and armor from the Kofun period to the introduction of firearms / Thom RichardsonaJapanese arms and armor after 1600 / Gregory IrvineaBushido ̄: the way of the warrior / Eric MeulienaCatalog : Helmets ; Masks ; Suits of armor ; Textiles and accessories ; Weaponry and battle ; Horse accoutrements ; The Mōri ensemble / Bernard Fournier-BourdieraComponents of an armor.  a"This extraordinary publication presents, for the first time, the samurai armor collection of the Ann and Gabriel Barbier-Mueller Museum in Dallas. The Barbier-Mueller has selectively amassed these pieces of armor over the past twenty-five years, ultimately forming one of the largest and most important collections of its kind in the world. It is composed of nearly three hundred objects, several of which are considered masterpieces, including suits of armor, helmets, masks, horse armor, and weaponry. The objects date from the 12th to the 19th century, with a particularly strong focus on Edo-period armor.  Offering an exciting look into the world of the samurai warrior, the book begins with an introduction by Morihiro Ogawa. Essays by prominent scholars in the field highlight topics such as the phenomenon of the warrior in Japan, the development of the samurai helmet, castle architecture, women in samurai culture, and Japanese horse armor. The book\'s final section consists of an extensive catalogue of objects, concentrating on 120 significant works in the collection. Lavishly illustrated in full color, each object is accompanied by an entry written by a scholar of Japanese armor."--Publisher\'s website1 aExpositionmParisnMusée du quai Branlyj2011j20121 aExpositionmQuébecnMusée de la civilisationj2012j20131 aSamurai armor from the Ann and Gabriel Barbier-Mueller Museum||316733965aThe Ann and Gabriel Barbier-Mueller museumcDallas, Tex311975940xCatalogues2rameau  312266187aArmures311934253yJapon311938837xCatalogues d\'exposition2rameau  311971627aSamouraïs311936165xCostume311938837xCatalogues d\'exposition2rameau  311934803aArmes311934253yJapon311938837xCatalogues d\'exposition2rameau  a739.709 52074v23 |312574114oISNI0000000081887045aOgawabMorihirof1946-....4070 |316676629oISNI0000000403284547aFournier-BourdierbBernard4070 |316733901oISNI0000000432705291aBarbier-MuellerbJ. Gabriel4340||313555967oISNI0000000406472404aMusée du quai Branly-Jacques ChiraccParis4070||312400860oISNI0000000404477586aMusée de la civilisationcQuébec, Canada4070 3aUSbOCoLCc20140108h7110454902marc21 0bDLC  5FR-751131010:42716420001001a2012-229160b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Littérature et art - MagasindO01623nam  2200253   450 001002100000003004700021039002800068100004100096101000800137102000700145105001800152106000600170200025800176210004700434215002300481225005600504300029000560410007000850710006600920801007000986930011501056930011001171930008801281FRBNF427927050000003http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb42792705z  oOPPa42797199d20121220  a20121116d2012    m  y0frey50      ba0 afre  aFR  aa   z   00|||  ar1 aDon Quichotte, Rudolf Noureev, Ballet de l\'OpérabTexte impriméeballet en un prologue et trois actes d\'après quelques épisodes du roman de Miguel de Cervantèse[programme, Opéra Bastille, première le 16 novembre 2012]fOpéra national de Paris  aPariscOpéra national de Parisdcop. 2012  a93 p.cill.d24 cm| a[Opéra national de Paris]e[programmes de ballets]  aDocument relatif au spectacle : Don Quichotte : bal