20 EUR  aFRb01215425 0a9782330001889  a20120305d2012    m  y0frey50      ba1 afrecgrc  aFR  a||||z   00|a|  ar1 aLa trilogie de la guerrebTexte impriméaProméthée enchaînéfEschylegtexte français d\'Olivier Py  aArlescActes Sud-Papiersdimpr. 2012e53-MayennegImpr. Floch  a1 vol. (111 p.)ccouv. ill.d21 cm| aActes Sud-Papiersx0298-0592  aRéunit : "Les Sept contre Thèbes" ; "Les suppliantes" ; "Les Perses" 0034230358tThéâtre (Paris. 1985)x0298-0592d2012  a882.01 (oeuvre)v23  a8022Cadre de classement de la Bibliographie nationale française |311888147oISNI0000000386855773aEschylef0525?-0456 av. J.-C.4070 |312265840oISNI0000000363513332aPybOlivierf1965-....4730 0aFRbFR-751131015c20120305gAFNORhFRBNF4261678600000082intermrc  5FR-751131010:42616786001001a88/1 ESCHy 2 tb759999999cTolbiac - Haut de Jardin - Littérature et art - Salle H - Libre accèsdN  5FR-751131010:42616786002001a2012-54804b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Littérature et art - MagasindO  5FR-751071001:42616786003001aT ESCHY Tb759999999cMaison Jean Vilar - Libre accèsdN03331cam  22004213  450 FRBNF435673550000001http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb43567355s  a9780878467815bhardcover  a0878467815bhardcover  a9780878467877bsoftcover  a0878467874bsoftcover  aOCoLC829900527  a20131206d2012    m  y0frey50      ba0 aeng  aUS  aa   z   00|y|  ar1 aThe postcard agebTexte impriméeselections from the Leonard A. Lauder collectionfLynda Klich and Benjamin Weiss  a1st ed.  aBostoncMuseum of fine artsd2012  a1 vol. (295 p.)cill. en noir et en coul.d25 cm  aPublié à l\'occasion d\'une exposition tenue au Museum of fine arts, Boston, du 24 octobre 2012 au 14 avril 2013  aBibliogr.  aAutre forme de titre : Selections from the Leonard A. Lauder Collection1 aDirector\'s foreword / Malcolm Rogers  ;  Messages from the postcard age / Leonard A. Lauder  ; Paris  ; The craze  ; Style  ; About town  ; Women  ; Famous and familiar  ; Power, speed and flight  ; Making the sale  ; Healthy bodies  ; Around the world  ; The Great War.  a"In the decades around 1900, postcards were Twitter, email, Flickr and Facebook, all wrapped into one. A postcard craze swept the world, and billions of cards were bought, mailed and pasted into albums. Many famous artists turned to the new medium, but one of the great pleasures and enigmas of postcards is how some of the most beautiful and interesting examples were made by artists whose names we barely know. Drawing on the riches of the Leonard A. Lauder Postcard Collection (probably the finest and most comprehensive collection of its type), this gorgeous book traces the historical and cultural themes--enthralling, exciting, and sometimes disturbing--of the modern age. The first general publication on the postcard as an artistic medium since the mid-1970s, The Postcard Age is organized thematically, with chapters devoted to urban life, the changing role of women, sports, celebrity, new technologies, the stylish collectors\' cards of Art Nouveau and World War I. The result is at once a vivid picture of the concerns and pastimes of the turn of the century and a sampler from the Lauder\'s vast archives."--[Source inconnue]1 aExpositionmBostonnMuseum of fine artsj2012j20131 aSelections from the Leonard A. Lauder Collection |314600638aLauderbLeonard A.f1933-....xCollections d\'art2rameau||311866613aMuseum of fine artscBoston, Mass311975940xCatalogues2rameau  311965925aCartes postalesxCollectionneurs et collections311931371yÉtats-Unis2rameau  311949215aCartes postales311934444xHistoire2rameau |316728360oISNI0000000373224438aWeissbBenjaminf19..-....cconservateur4070 |316728363oISNI0000000410333570aKlichbLynda4070||311866613oISNI0000000122918830aMuseum of fine artscBoston, Mass.4070 3aUSbOCoLCc20131206h8299005272marc21 0bLVB  5FR-751021001:43567355001001aYD2-19610-8b7