rs of Leo IV in the Collectio Britannica --a\'We are between the hammer and the anvil\': Hincmar in the crisis of 875 /Clémentine Bernard-ValetteaHincmar\'s influence during Louis the Stammerer\'s reign /Margaret McCarthyaHincmar and his Roman legal sources /Simon Corcorana\'Hincmar et la loi\' revisited: on Hincmar\'s use of capitularies /Philippe DepreuxaThe bishop and the law, according to Hincmar\'s Life of Saint Remigius /Marie-Céline IsaïaaFamily order and kingship according to Hincmar /Sylvie Joyea\'The praetor does concern himself with trifles\': Hincmar, the polyptych of St-Remi of Rheims and the slaves of Courtisols /Josiane BarbierAppendixaThe nota and the structure of the entry for Courtisols in the Paris manuscript --aHincmar\'s parish priests /Charles WestaHeresy in the flesh: Gottschalk of Orbais and the predestination controversy in the archdiocese of Rheims /Matthew Bryan GillisaHincmar, priests and Pseudo-Isidore. The case of Trising in context /Mayke de JongAppendixaLetter from Hincmar of Rheims to Pope Hadrian II, spring 871.  a"Archbishop Hincmar of Rheims (d.882) is a crucial figure for early medieval European history. As an archbishop for nearly forty years, Hincmar shaped the times in which he lived, advising and admonishing kings, playing a leading role in the Frankish church, and intervening in a range of political and doctrinal disputes. His role in the controversial attempts by King Lothar II to divorce his queen Theutberga has particularly interested researchers. Hincmar also shaped how ninth-century events would later be seen by historians up to the present day by writing historical accounts such as the Annals of St-Bertin, and by carefully preserving dossiers of material for posterity. He is a key source for political, social and religious history in the period, providing information on everything from papal politics to the abduction of women and the role of parish priests. This book puts the archbishop himself centre-stage, bringing together the latest international research across the spectrum of his varied activities, as history-writer, estate administrator, hagiographer, canonist, pastorally-engaged bishop and politically-minded royal advisor. For the first time since Jean Devisses magisterial studies of the 1970s, it offers a three-dimensional examination of a controversial figure whose actions and writings in different fields are often studied in isolation, at the cost of a holistic appreciation. Combining research from recognised experts ... as well as early-career historians, it will be an essential companion for all those interested in the Carolingian world, and early medieval Europe more broadly."--P. [4] of cover |312083500aHincmarf0806?-0882312061148xActes de congrès2rameau  311974301aÉglise catholiquexÉvêques311935764xBiographies311993883z9e siècle312061148xActes de congrès2rameau  311954018aÉvêques311931476yFrance311941609yReims (Marne)311935764xBiographies311993883z9e siècle312061148xActes de congrès2rameau |316728696oISNI0000000123472922aStonebRachel4340 |316736031oISNI0000000400094158aWestbCharlesf1979-....4340 3aUSbOCoLCc20161208h9071141742marc21 0bBTCTAgrda  5FR-751131007:45095883001001a2016-250916b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Philosophie, histoire, sciences de l\'homme - MagasindO04134cam  2200349   450 FRBNF442321630000002http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb44232163n  a9781441141903bhardbackbalkaline paper  a1441141901bhardbackbalkaline paper  a9781441159304bpaperbackbalkaline paper  a1441159304bpaperbackbalkaline paperz9781441148407bepdfz9781441111661bePub  a1441111662  a9781441111661  aOCoLC858353573  a20150622d2014    m  y0engy50      ba0 aeng  aGB  ay   z   00|y|  az1 aQueer cities, queer culturesbTexte impriméeEurope since 1945fedited by Matt Cook and Jennifer V. Evans  aLondonaNew YorkcBloomsburyd2014  a1 vol. (xii, 313 p.)d25 cm  aIncludes bibliographical references and index1 aIntroduction / Matt Cook (Birkbeck, University of London, UK) &amp; Jennifer Evans (Carleton University, Canada)  ;  The queer margins of Spanish cities, 1939-2010 / Richard Cleminson (University of Leeds, UK), Rosa Maria Medina Doménech (University of Granada, Spain) &amp; Isabel Vélez (independent scholar)  ; Capital stories : local lives in queer London / Matt Cook  ; The queer road to Frisind : Copenhagen 1945-2012 / Peter Edelberg (University of Copenhagen, Denmark)  ; Harmless kisses and infinite loops : making space for queer place in 21st century Berlin / Jennifer Evans  ; From Stalinist pariahs to subjects of \'managed democracy\' : queers in Moscow 1945 to the present / Dan Healey (University of Oxford, UK)  ; Queer Amsterdam 1945-2010 / Gert Hekma (University of Amsterdam, Netherlands)  ; Ljubljana : the tales from the queer margins of the city / Roman Kuhar (University of Ljubljana, Slovenia)  ; Mapping/unmapping : the making of queer Athens / Dimitris Papanikolaou (Oxford University, UK)  ; Istanbul : queer desires between Muslim tradition and global pop / Ralph Poole (Salzburg University, Austria)  ; Queering Budapest / Judit Takács (Hungarian Academy of Sciences)  ; Two cities of Helsinki? : one liberally gay and one practically queer? / Antu Sorainen (Academy of Finland)  ; Paris : \'resting on its laurels\'? / Florence Tamagne (University of Lille, France)  ; \'Gays who cannot properly be gay\' : queer Muslims in the neoliberal European city / Fatima El-Tayeb (University of California, San Diego)  ; Seeing like a queer city / Tom Boellstorff (University of California, Irvine).  a"Through a series of urban case studies, Queer Cities, Queer Cultures examines the articulation of particular subcultures and forms of expression with the broader stories we tell about postwar Europe and particular watershed moments. It considers queer life in the selected cities in relation to the advent and end of Cold War polarization, and considers the degree to which the iconic events of 1945, 1968, and 1989 influenced the social and sexual climate of the ensuing decades. It raises questions about the form and structure of the 1960s sexual revolution, and forces us to think about how we define sexual liberalization and where, how and on whose terms it occurs. The book also explores the role of America in shaping particular forms of subculture; the significance of changes in legal codes; modes of queer consumption and displays of community; the difficult fit of queer (as opposed to gay and lesbian) politics in liberal democracies; the challenge of AIDS; and the arrival of the Internet"  315832267aThéorie queer311931301yEurope312433520z1945-....2rameau  311932034aHomosexualité311931301yEurope312433520z1945-....2rameau  311947346aLesbianisme311931301yEurope312433520z1945-....2rameau  311953336aTranssexualisme311931301yEurope312433520z1945-....2rameau 3aUSbOCoLCc20150622h8583535732marc21 0bDLCgrda  5FR-751131007:44232163001001a2015-106042b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Philosophie, histoire, sciences de l\'homme - MagasindO01559cam  2200313   450 001002100000003004700021010003700068020001700105073001800122100004100140101001300181102000700194105001800201106000600219200021800225210008400443215003900527225003400566410006400600461003500664500008900699676001500788686007000803700006800873702005600941702006200997801007001059930011601129FRBNF426868760000002http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb42686876b  a978-2-246-79376-2bbr.d9,50 EUR  aFRb01241226 0a9782246793762  a20120612d2012    m  y0frey50      ba1 afrecita  aFR  a||||z   00|y|  ar1 aVies des artistesh2bTexte impriméevies des plus excellents peintres, sculpteurs et architectesfGiorgio Vasarigtraduction de l\'italien par Léopold Leclanchégrevue, annotée et préfacée par Benoît Fuchs  aPariscB. Grassetdimpr. 2012e27-Mesnil-sur-l\'EstréegImpr. CPI Firmin-Didot  a1 vol. (253 p.)ccouv. ill.d19 cm| aLes cahiers rougesx0756-7170 0034232845tLes Cahiers rouges (Paris. 1983)x0756-7170d2012 0042713545tVies des artistesv211312027543aVite dei più eccellenti pittori, scultori e architettorimfrançaisk2012  a709.45v23  a9202Cadre de classement de la Bibliographie nationale française |311927728oISNI0000000121309590aVasaribGiorgiof1511-15744070 |316613672oISNI0000000374859400aFuchsbBenoît4340 |312188042oISNI0000000006561942aLeclanchébLéopold4730 0aFRbFR-751131015c20120612gAFNORhFRBNF4268687600000022intermrc  5FR-751131010:42686876001001a2012-135688b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Littérature et art - MagasindO04036cam  22003373  450 FRBNF436757360000005http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb43675736h  a9780230244177brel.  a0230244173  aOCoLC748328926  a20131127d2012    m  y0engy50      ba0 aeng  aGB  aa   z   00|y|  az1 aOlympics games, mega-events, and civil societiesbTexte impriméeglobalization, environment, resistancefedited by Graeme Hayes and John Karamichas  aHoundmills, Basingstoke, HampshireaNew York, NYcPalgrave Macmilland2012  axiii, 292 p.cill., mapd23 cm| aGlobal culture and sport  aIncludes bibliographical references (p. 262-285) and index1 aIntroduction: sports mega-events, sustainable development, and civil societies / Graeme Hayes, John Karamichas  ; The four \'Cs\' of sports mega-events: capitalism, connections, citizenship and contradictions / John Horne  ; Civilizing Beijing: social beautification, civility and citizenship at the 2008 Olympics / Anne-Marie Broudehoux  ; Istanbul\'s Olympic challenge: a passport for Europe? / Jean-François Polo  ; The failed bid for Lyon \'68 and France\'s Winter Olympics from Grenoble \'68 to Annecy 2018: French politics, civil society and Olympic mega-events / Hugh Dauncey  ; The role of environmental issues in mega-events planning and management processes: which factors count? / Pietro Caratti, Ludovico Ferraguto  ; Sustainability as global norm: the greening of mega-events in China / Arthur P.J. Mol, Lei Zhang  ; Olympic Games as an opportunity for the ecological modernization of the host nation: the cases of Sydney 2000 and Athens 2004 / John Karamichas  ; What happens when Olympic bids fail? Sustainable development and Paris 2012 / Graeme Hayes  ; Olympic Games, conflicts and social movements: the case of Torino 2006 / Egidio Dansero ... [et al.]  ; Vancouver 2010: the saga of Eagleridge Bluffs / David Whitson  ; Resisting the torch / Xavier Renou  ; Conclusion: sports mega-events: disputed places, systemic contradictions and critical moments / Graeme Hayes, John Karamichas.  aThis volume explores sports mega-events, their social, political, and cultural characters, the value systems that they inscribe and draw on, the claims they make on us and the claims the organisers make for them, the spatial and ethical relationships they create, and the responses of civil societies to them. Our premise is that sports mega-events are not simply sporting or cultural phenomena. They are also political and economic events, characterised by the generation and projection of symbolic meanings -- most obviously over the nature of statehood, economic power, and of collective cultural identity -- and by social conflict, especially over land use, and over the extent and contours of public spending commitments. Because of their peculiar spatial and temporal organization, they raise questions about the relationships between global cultural and economic flows and particular local and national spaces. Because of their evolutionary characteristics, they ask us to consider not simply the time of the event but of the effects of the event on the long-term direction, implementation, and consequences of public policy. -- Publisher description 0042619924tGlobal culture and sport seriesd2012  311939226aJeux olympiques311975691xAspect social2rameau  311939226aJeux olympiques311959574xAspect environnemental2rameau  316250159aSports et mondialisation2rameau |314613714oISNI0000000045730294aHayesbGraemef1967-....4340 |316725971oISNI0000000357328878aKaramichasbJohnf1975-....4340 3aUSbOCoLCc20131127h7483289262marc21 0bDLC  5FR-751131007:43675736001001a2013-399382b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Philosophie, histoire, sciences de l\'homme - MagasindO01848cam  2200349   450 FRBNF435004510000004http://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb43500451r  a978-2-204-09985-1bbr.d48 EUR  aFRb01268365 0a9782204099851  a20121211d2012    m  y0frey50      ba1 alatafreclat  aFR  a||||z   00|||  ar1 aInstruction des laïcsh01iLivres I-II, 16bTexte impriméfJonas d\'Orléansgintroduction, texte, traduction et notes par Odile Dubreucq  aPariscles Éd. du Cerfd2012e80-AbbevillegImpr. F. Paillart  a1 vol. (467 p.)d20 cm| aSources chrétiennesx0750-1978vn° 549  aTexte latin et trad. française en regard  aBibliogr. p. 17-31 0034232178tSources chrétiennes (Paris)x0750-1978v549 0043505630tInstruction des laïcsv111316650460aDe institutione laicalimlatin-françaisk2012-  a248.4v23  a2202Cadre de classement de la Bibliographie nationale française |312162782oISNI000000009418965XaJonas d\'Orléansf0780?-084.4070 |312341706oISNI0000000000411775aDubreucqbOdilef1959-....4340 0aFRbFR-751131015c20121211gAFNORhFRBNF4350045100000042intermrc  5FR-751131007:43500451001001a2012-355891b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Philosophie, histoire, sciences de l\'homme - MagasindO  5FR-751131007:43500451002001a270.005 SOUR 549b759999999cTolbiac - Rez de Jardin - Philosophie, histoire, sciences de l\'homme - Salle K - Libre accèsdN  5FR-751131007:43500451003001a248 JONA I1b759999999cTolbiac - Haut de Jardin - Philosophie, histoire, sciences de l\'homme - Salle J - Libre accèsdNvvol. 101783cam  2200349   450 FRBNF43671051000000